Z||000000||nivlek68||07-13-2000||01:23 AM|||| i have a 86 2m4,auto,2.5 coupe. i would like to know if a 3.4 ? camaro\firebird would bolt to the trans. i know there will be other mods that will be needed. planing on a swap later on down the road.any info will be gladly accepted.  nevlek68 wondering<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||ThatRickGuy||07-13-2000||07:13 AM||||Check out Ed's page for the fiero factory, I don't have the link readily available, but look into the 3.4/auto and expencive (both very recent) threads. You'll need an 88 or later flex plate for the 3.4, 84-87 fiero engine mount, 84-87 AC bracket, the starter needs to be swaped to the other side, and there is a small area on the block that has to be trimmed so it'll fit against the tranny.||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||07-13-2000||07:26 AM||||The ECM and engine wiring harness needs changed over to a V6 auto computer too.||||reg||1
Z||000003||nivlek68||07-13-2000||09:51 AM||||do need to switch the comp. from donner car and keep mine too? i ceck out the pontiac web site and the new fire bird has.<BR> 3.8L 3800 SFI V6 , HP 200@5,200rpm , torque 225ftlbs@4,000rpm <BR>  would that work on a auto or would i have to go standard <BR>                    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000004||Oreif||07-13-2000||10:02 AM||||You can use any Fiero trans with any engine swap. Archie uses the stock Fiero auto trans on his V-8 swaps. Although if the V-8 goes over 300 hp he usually has the auto trans beefed up just to be on the safe side. With a 3800 swap you can go to the 4-spd auto which is suppose to be a real nice match for the 3800.||||reg||1
